# Rank 1521 / CVE-2021-25931: OpenNMS' requisition UI concatenated
# $scope values into growl notification messages, which the growl
# directive renders as HTML, so a requisition name or node label
# carrying markup executed in the operator's browser (cross-site
# scripting, CWE-79; NMS-13231 backport). The controllers in
# core/web-assets/src/main/assets/js/apps/onms-requisitions/lib/
# scripts/controllers did `growl.success('The definition for the
# requisition ' + $scope.foreignSource + ' has been saved.')` and a
# dozen siblings -- every $scope-derived field flows raw into the
# notification -- while one path wrapped the message in $sanitize
# (HTML sanitising, wrong for a text context). Pool commit eb08b5ed4c
# is the real fix (COMMIT_OK -- "NMS-13231: Backport Security Issues
# from Last Month"): every interpolation is wrapped in lodash's
# _.escape($scope...) and the $sanitize calls are removed (escaping,
# not sanitising, is the control a text notification needs). No pool
# correction.
#
# ATTENTION, member-field provenance and an unbound notification
# sink. Both halves exist in the corpus: _.escape is a bound
# core.HtmlEscape control (mfb63017a.vyql:2843, callee.path ~=
# "_.escape") and string concatenation into a rendered message is
# HtmlRender in spirit -- but the source never labels ($scope.foreignSource
# is a framework-object member read, the same boundary ranks 1518
# and 1545 recorded) and the sink never fires (growl.success is a
# project directive call, not markup), so no taint path forms.
# Measured on the real code: scanning ForeignSource.js (the
# controllers directory file) reports zero findings at both
# revisions. When framework-object provenance lands, the raw concat
# reports and the _.escape form suppresses -- the control binding
# already exists. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. No definition change
# shipped. Spec cve_rank1521 records the raw growl concat and the
# _.escape-wrapped form, both asserting reject VYQL-INJ-004: when
# member-field vocabulary lands, the raw form must flip to expect.

test "rank1521: requisition names flow raw into notifications"
  lang javascript
  file core/web-assets/src/main/assets/js/apps/onms-requisitions/lib/scripts/controllers/ForeignSource.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  angular.module('onms-requisitions').controller('ForeignSourceController', function($scope, growl) {
      $scope.save = function() {
          RequisitionsService.saveForeignSource($scope.foreignSourceDef).then(
              function() {
                  growl.success('The definition for the requisition ' + $scope.foreignSource + ' has been saved.');
              }
          );
      };

      $scope.reset = function() {
          RequisitionsService.resetForeignSource($scope.foreignSource).then(
              function() {
                  growl.success('The foreign source definition for ' + $scope.foreignSource + 'has been reseted.');
              }
          );
      };
  });
  ```

test "rank1521: the fix escapes every interpolation"
  lang javascript
  file core/web-assets/src/main/assets/js/apps/onms-requisitions/lib/scripts/controllers/ForeignSource.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  angular.module('onms-requisitions').controller('ForeignSourceController', function($scope, growl) {
      $scope.save = function() {
          RequisitionsService.saveForeignSource($scope.foreignSourceDef).then(
              function() {
                  growl.success('The definition for the requisition ' + _.escape($scope.foreignSource) + ' has been saved.');
              }
          );
      };

      $scope.reset = function() {
          RequisitionsService.resetForeignSource($scope.foreignSource).then(
              function() {
                  growl.success('The foreign source definition for ' + _.escape($scope.foreignSource) + 'has been reseted.');
              }
          );
      };
  });
  ```
